{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q014_paper_example_reclassification_pa1492","answer":"In SCOP 1.69, PA1492 (1t1j) was not grouped with nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase (1f8y). It was a structural-genomics protein of unknown function placed in its own separate fold/superfamily, apart from the nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase group. This 1.69 placement is from my recollection of Andreeva et al. 2008, not verified, because the SCOPe API does not cover SCOP 1.69.

In the current SCOPe (2.08, with the periodic update 2.08-2026-08-16), the two are in the same superfamily but different families. 1t1j domains d1t1ja1 and d1t1jb1 (sunids 106249 and 106250) are in c.23.14.2, family 'Hypothetical protein PA1492' (sunid 110461), species Pseudomonas aeruginosa. 1f8y domains d1f8ya_ and d1f8yb_ (sunids 31395 and 31396) are in c.23.14.1, family 'N-deoxyribosyltransferase' (sunid 52310), protein 'Nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase' (sunid 52311), species Lactobacillus leichmannii. Both share class c (alpha/beta), fold c.23 and superfamily c.23.14 'N-(deoxy)ribosyltransferase-like' (sunid 52309).

So the change is that PA1492 was brought into the same fold and superfamily as 1f8y. A shared superfamily implies a probable common evolutionary origin, supported by structure and function. The separate families reflect too little sequence similarity for a single family. This does not show PA1492 has nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase activity: its function remains unknown, so 1f8y's function or active-site/ligand assignments should not be transferred, and 1f8y should not be treated as a close template. The 1t1j domains d1t1ja2 and d1t1jb2 are in l.1.1.1, a non-domain artifact class for short tag regions, not part of the structural classification. The classification is release-specific; both entries are classified in 2.08.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/releases","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1t1j","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1f8y","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1t1j/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1f8y/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1f8ya_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110463","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52312","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110462","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52311","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110461","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/52310","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=c.23.14","pretrained knowledge of Andreeva et al. 2008"]}]}
